MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_001: I came here today to ask a favor of you.
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_002: Ohhh, I am deluged with work, I'm afraid. Is it\nimportant?
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_003: It is. I've heard you're a well-known author, skilled at\nweaving stories.
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_004: I understand that stories can entertain people—no\nmatter what is happening around them.
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_005: The villagers in Kunlun could use such distractions.\nI want to learn how to do what you do.
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_006: If it brings even the slightest relief to their\nchallenging lives, it would mean so much. Teach me.
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_007: Mm, no.
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_008: Wh-why not?
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_009: You cannot learn writing by being taught.
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_010: You just...do it! Let your heart spill over with feeling,\nand watch the seepage splash onto the page.
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_011: But I don't know the first thing about writing. So,\nwhere should I begin?
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_012: I would say "figure it out on your own," but you\nappear to be hellbent not to.
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_013: This much I'll tell you: good, vivid writing always\nbegins with an understanding of people.
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_014: To practice, why not ask someone to tell you\ntheir story? Someone other than me.
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_015: I see! Thank you. I'll give it a try.
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_016: She's so sincere. That might be a strength for her\nwriting... Only time will tell.
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_017: Ah, what a productive interview! I can hardly\nwait to manifest it in my work.
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_018: Dante, I want to thank you for your advice.
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_019: Anatolia, hello! That's a hefty stack of papers.\nWith script on them, I see.
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_020: Mhm! I listened to people's concerns and\nexperiences, and then I compiled everything.
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_021: You mean those pages are all...from your interviews?\nHow did you get so many?
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_022: Well, I practice divination for the people of Dagsion.\nThey usually share their stories with me.
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_023: After listening to what they shared, I asked for the\npeople's permission to be subjects for my writing.
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_024: {SetColor=Gray}Here I am going out and asking subjects for\ninterviews.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_025: {SetColor=Gray}Meanwhile, she's devised a system whereby they\ncome to her. It's brilliant!{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_026: {SetColor=Gray}It's like a river overflowing with ghosh, a storm of\ngolden apples—the sweet fruitage of IDEAS!{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_027: Are you OK?
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_C_028: Of course I'm not jealous!
MID_SE_Anh_Dan_B: 
